<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — app-wide Apple privacy manifest (#1449)

  ELI5: A form Apple makes every App Store app fill in that says "here's
  whether we track people across other apps/websites, here's what personal
  info we collect (if any), and here's exactly why we use a short list of
  sensitive system APIs" — checked by Xcode/App Store Connect at archive
  and submission time.

  DETAILED: Covers the `iHymns` target — the universal iOS/iPadOS/macOS/
  visionOS app shell (`appApple/project.yml`'s `iHymns` target,
  `supportedDestinations: [iOS, macOS, visionOS]`). This is the ONLY app
  shell that currently reaches any code using a "required reason" API (see
  the `NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes` entry below) — `iHymnsTV`/`iHymnsWatch`
  still render only `PhaseZeroSkeletonView`, and `iHymnsWidgets` doesn't
  even import `IHFeatures` yet, so all three ship their own EMPTY manifests
  (`Apps/iHymnsTV/Sources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`,
  `Apps/iHymnsWatch/Sources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`,
  `Apps/iHymnsWidgets/Sources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`) rather than copying
  this one — a manifest must be ACCURATE to what that specific bundle
  actually does, not a blanket copy-paste (this issue's own "accuracy
  matters more than completeness-theatre" framing). Each of those three
  gets the identical `NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults` entry added
  the moment Phase 1 actually wires it to `IHSettingsStore`/etc.

  This file was written by hand after auditing the ENTIRE `appApple/`
  source tree for every required-reason API category Apple's 2024 policy
  gates (`grep`-swept for `UserDefaults`, file-timestamp APIs
  [`creationDate`/`contentModificationDate`/`fileModificationDate`/
  `getattrlist`/`attributesOfItem`/`stat`/`lstat`/`fstat`], disk-space APIs
  [`volumeAvailableCapacity*`/`systemFreeSize`/`statfs`/`statvfs`], and
  system-boot-time APIs [`systemUptime`/`mach_absolute_time`]) — see each
  section below for exactly which files justify which declaration, and
  which categories were found UNUSED and correctly omitted.

  Reference: Apple's "Describing use of required reason API" —
  https://developer.apple.com/documentation/bundleresources/describing-use-of-required-reason-api
  and "Privacy manifest files" —
  https://developer.apple.com/documentation/bundleresources/privacy_manifest_files.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      NSPrivacyTracking = false: iHymns does no cross-app/cross-website
      tracking (Apple's definition — linking data to a third party's data
      for targeted advertising/ad measurement, or sharing with a data
      broker). #189's analytics pipeline (`IHAnalyticsService.swift`) is
      first-party-only, consent-gated (`IHSettingsStore.analyticsConsentEnabled`,
      `ihAnalyticsConsentEnabled` key), and — as of this audit — its ONLY
      conformer, `IHAnalyticsLogSink` (`IHAppSupport/IHAnalyticsSink.swift`),
      is a `#if DEBUG`-only `os.Logger` call: nothing is transmitted
      off-device at all in Release builds (no `URLSession`-based sink
      exists yet; that's #1448, still pending). No App Tracking Transparency
      (`ATTrackingManager`) code exists anywhere in the tree either — grepped
      and confirmed zero hits. `NSPrivacyTrackingDomains` is correctly empty
      to match.
    -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <!--
      NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes = []: genuinely empty, not an oversight.
      The app collects no PII from the user (no account-required signup for
      the core reading experience; native sign-in, where it exists, is
      email-magic-link only and its token lives in the Keychain, not
      analytics). #189's analytics currently records nothing off-device (see
      the `NSPrivacyTracking` comment above) — the moment #1448 gives it a
      real transmitting sink, this array gets a
      `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeProductInteraction` entry with
      `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked = false` and
      `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking = false` (first-party, anonymous,
      consent-gated product-interaction counts only) — NOT before, per this
      issue's own "reflect reality" instruction.
    -->
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>

    <!--
      NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes — audited every one of Apple's required-
      reason categories against the full `appApple/Packages/iHymnsKit/Sources`
      + `appApple/Apps/*/Sources` tree. Only ONE category has a real,
      first-party usage:

      UserDefaults (NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults, reason CA92.1
      — "access user defaults to read/write information that is only
      accessible to the app itself"; the other three approved reason codes
      for this category don't fit: 1C8F.1 is for an App Group container
      shared with other apps/extensions from the SAME developer, which
      nothing here uses; AC6B.1 is MDM-managed app configuration; C56D.1 is
      a third-party SDK wrapping UserDefaults on the app's behalf — this is
      first-party app code calling `UserDefaults.standard` directly).
      Concrete call sites (`IHFeatures` target, `IHymnsKit` package):
        - `IHSettingsStore.swift` (init `defaults: UserDefaults = .standard`)
          — appearance theme, colour-vision-deficiency mode, dyslexia
          reading mode, analytics-consent flag, onboarding-seen flag, API
          environment override.
        - `RecentSearchesStore.swift` — the last ~10 distinct catalogue
          search terms (`ihRecentCatalogueSearches` key).
        - `RecentlyViewedStore.swift` — the last ~12 recently-opened songs,
          JSON-encoded (`ihRecentlyViewedSongs` key).
        - `UsageActivityStore.swift` (#1446) — the LOCAL-ONLY "Your Activity"
          dashboard's day-by-day distinct-songs-opened counts + per-song
          open counts, JSON-encoded (`ihUsageActivity` key). Written from
          `AppRootViewModel+Activity.swift`'s `recordRecentlyViewed(_:)`
          (the SAME successful-song-load hook `RecentlyViewedStore` above
          already uses), read by `UsageStatsViewModel`/`UsageStatsView`
          (Settings → "Your Activity"). This is NOT a new collected-data
          type — see the `NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes` comment above and
          that screen's own header: on-device display of a user's own data
          is not "collection," and this store is never read by
          `IHAnalyticsService`/any sink, nor gated on
          `analyticsConsentEnabled`.
      All four are reached from this target via `AppRootViewModel.swift`,
      `RootContainerView.swift`, and `Apps/iHymns/Sources/IHymnsApp.swift`.

      Every OTHER required-reason category was checked and found UNUSED,
      so is correctly OMITTED (not declared with a bogus reason) rather
      than included "just in case":
        - File timestamps (`NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp`) —
          every `FileManager` call in the tree (`OfflineStore.swift`,
          `OfflineStore+MediaCache.swift`, `MediaDownloadViewModel.swift`,
          `AppRootViewModel+Live.swift`) is a non-gated existence/write/
          delete/directory-creation call; nothing reads a creation/
          modification timestamp.
        - Disk space (`NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace`) — no
          `volumeAvailableCapacity*`/`systemFreeSize`/`statfs` call
          anywhere; the Storage & Offline screen (`OfflineStorageView.swift`)
          reports the app's OWN cache size via `SUM(...)` SQL aggregates
          (`OfflineStore+SavedSongs.swift`/`+MediaCache.swift`), never the
          volume's free space.
        - System boot time (`NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime`) —
          no `systemUptime`/`mach_absolute_time` call anywhere.
        - Active keyboards — no `UITextInputMode`/`activeInputModes` call
          anywhere.

      GRDB.swift (the SQLite engine backing `IHPersistence.OfflineStore`,
      pinned exact at 7.11.1, `Package.swift`) ships its OWN
      `PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy` (`.build/checkouts/GRDB.swift/GRDB/
      PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`) declaring ZERO required-reason API usage of
      its own — nothing to merge in from that dependency.
    -->
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
